---
name: animate-pixel-sprite
description: Animate accepted native pixel-art masters with local or full-body motion, generated missing poses and an exact PNG timeline. Also use for one requested cel or assembly of existing poses; review real playback and preserve native identity without silently redesigning the master.
---

# Animate Pixel Sprite

Read `references/runtime.md` before using tools or scripts. Animate accepted native pixels. Canonical output is unchanged native PNG drawings plus an explicit millisecond timeline; sheets, GIFs and viewers are derived playback artifacts.

## Choose scope and modes

Read `references/project-contract.md`. Inspect actual accepted native masters, identity/profile, relevant views, action readiness and approval evidence. A study is not a native master; resolve missing native acceptance through `refine-pixel-art` and ask only for blocking choices.
- **Standalone animation, single cel or pose assembly:** Use the compact record/helper contract in `references/standalone-records.md`. Keep `project.json`/`profile.json` for pipeline helpers; several drawings do not by themselves require a full run directory or portable bundle.
- **Requested multi-stage workflow, cross-session continuation or portable handoff:** Read `references/run-records.md` and `references/portable-handoff.md`. Check supplied bundles and reconstruct context from actual assets and records. Continue existing counters and approval scope, not a new allowance or hidden parent instructions.

Choose task mode: **complete-loop** carries a requested animation through missing art and playback review; **single-cel** makes one requested drawing; **reuse-existing-poses** only assembles supplied art and never authorizes new generation. Keep missing mandatory phases explicit.

Choose motion mode before generation:
- **local:** Predeclare a mask/regions covering the whole original moving part, swept envelope and vacated area, preserving every outside RGBA pixel. Read `references/local-motion.md` and complete coverage preflight **before generating or composing local art**. Protected old outline pixels can remain as stray fragments; exact outside-mask preservation alone is insufficient
- **full_body:** Use `references/full-body-motion.md`. Permit articulation while preserving identity/style, camera, root/ground model and apparent scale under declared tolerances. Do not impose a local mask or identical silhouette boxes

Keep native size, palette roles/limit, alpha, padding and user limits fixed. Set shared call/repair allocations before generation; failed/cancelled/pending starts count across stages and sessions. Honor reserved user checkpoints; otherwise quoted delegation of the finished artifact can cover necessary gates. Record actual assistant acceptance, never user approval of unseen pixels.

## Plan drawings separately from timing

1. Name the observable action and minimum semantic phases. Read `references/action-continuity.md` for linked actions and record anatomical roles, support, contact and occlusion. A blink, bob or raised hand does not substitute for a distinct requested action. Full-body cycles need appropriate contact/passing/extreme poses and root behavior.
2. Choose the smallest readable drawing set and separately its ordered timeline and holds. Distinct drawings are decoded RGBA content, not filenames; repeated holds do not create drawings. Declare the loop return rather than assuming equal endpoints make smooth motion.
3. Fill `pose-plan.json` with project, motion mode, semantic IDs, sources/status, order, durations, readability/contact criteria and budget allocation. Use multiples of 10 ms for exact GIF timing. Generate the hardest distinctive primary-action key first; verify viability and reserve bounded repairs before spending on easy embellishments.

## Make and review new drawings

4. Use `scripts/native_reference.py` for an exact integer nearest-neighbor enlargement of the accepted native master and inspect it. This is the **primary imagegen pixel/identity reference**, linked to the original native hash. Add accepted native action keys/neighbors for continuity; concepts and view studies are supplementary. Inspect all inputs and state reference/limb roles explicitly.
5. Record each start with exact prompt, actual tool arguments and reference roles/hashes before imagegen. Request one intended pose per call. Dependent phases need master plus an accepted key/neighbor; neither independent generation from rest nor chaining from only the last generated image preserves continuity reliably. Preserve all returned originals and rejections unchanged in unique attempt paths; repairs get new paths and count against the same caps.
6. Measure actual output dimensions/grid/crop before `prepare_pixels.sh --project project.json`; see `references/pixel-tooling.md`. Reference size does not guarantee returned geometry. Use approved palette and matching measured grid lock, or document an equivalent full-canvas transform. Never independently trim/recenter, stretch a wrong aspect or shift poses to hide misalignment.
7. **Before local composition, follow `references/local-motion.md`:** verify actual motion and erasure fit the predeclared whole-part/envelope/vacated coverage, inspect alignment, compose only generated selected RGBA and review master→key plus adjacent composites. Undercoverage or protected remnants block acceptance; preserve evidence and require a documented replan instead of silently widening the mask. Full-body mode retains the whole normalized drawing and reviews identity/root/contact/scale, never local patching as a shortcut.
8. Follow the hardest-key independent checkpoint in `references/visual-review.md` before dependent frames; supplied-pose reuse follows the same policy without authorizing generation. Review each native phase and new adjacent pair/triple for readable action, contact/material chains, limb count, support roles, identity and palette-role continuity. Required-phase duplicates or ambiguous action fail. Repair the exact observed criterion through imagegen using accepted neighbors within caps. No manual cleanup or code-drawn replacements. At exhaustion retain `needs_revision`/incomplete, never approve failure to advance.

## Package, observe, deliver

9. Fill accepted paths, hashes and review/approval evidence in the pose plan. `pixel_pipeline.py plan` validates and packages; `pack` accepts a direct manifest. Missing required poses and shared-config contradictions must fail rather than be skipped. Single-cel work uses static scope; it does not pretend to complete a loop. For a requested portable single-cel handoff, use the refinement-stage identity/master/pose mapping in `references/portable-handoff.md`, without an invented timeline or playback claim.
10. Check dimensions, alpha, palette union, margins, drawing/entry counts, timing, transitions/wraparound, local protected pixels or full-body geometry, source/master hashes and decoded GIF fidelity. Technical pass cannot certify identity or motion.
11. Follow `references/visual-review.md`, including a fresh final independent checkpoint: inspect each native drawing, contact sheet, transitions and wraparound, then intended-speed playback at native size and integer enlargement. Distinguish launched playback, sampled screenshots and actually observed complete loops; unavailable evidence stays `unverified`. Review action, face, articulation/contact, flashes/jitter, holds, seams/footing and closure. Static review alone is not playback review.
12. Record timing/order revisions and export a new version. Artwork changes still use imagegen and consume caps. Preserve the accepted master byte-for-byte and keep failures visible.

Deliver requested native PNGs, exact timeline, useful playback previews and compact provenance/review records. State native size, entries, unique drawings, duration, budget used, separate technical/visual results, playback evidence level and limitations. Success requires the requested action and adequate playback evidence, not technical pass alone. For requested full/continuation delivery add and check the portable bundle; preserve the complete playback directory tree so viewer links survive relocation, never flatten linked files into hashed names.
